WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Thanks for joining us. This is OmniView, Episode 92, Balance News Perspectives.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.920
Today is June 24th, 2026. Today's stories, multiple viewpoints, your call.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.800
US Senate's rare bipartisan vote to limit war powers on Iran test the balance between

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.380
executive action and congressional oversight in ongoing Middle East conflicts.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.520
The US Senate voted in favor of a resolution calling for limits on presidential

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.920
authority regarding military action against Iran. Several Republicans joined Democrats in the

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:38.540
measure which the White House described as symbolic. Negotiators continue working toward a

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.980
potential agreement within 60 days amid disputes over nuclear inspections. The resolution reflects

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:50.540
institutional concerns about prolonged military engagement without fresh legislative approval.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.420
Deutsch Wellet coverage shows supporters in both parties emphasize restoring checks on executive

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:01.460
decisions that could expand into broader conflict. Critics within the administration,

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:07.800
as reported by Al Jazeera, view the step as an unnecessary constraint that weakens leverage during

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.100
active talks. Treasury and defense officials maintain that sustained pressure through sanctions

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:18.460
and military posture has brought Iran to the table. Congressional backers of the resolution

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.740
counter that unchecked executive latitude has historically led to mission creep.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.020
What specific language in the resolution distinguishes it from previous non-binding measures?

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:35.420
Shifting now to healthcare accountability in Britain, families affected by care at Nottingham

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:42.240
University Hospital's NHS Trust await a major independent review expected to outline systemic

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:48.400
failings linked to deaths and harm. The report is scheduled to examine how repeated incidents were

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:55.240
handled over several years. BBC News notes that bereaved families and patient advocates argue the

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.460
review must produce concrete accountability measures rather than repeat earlier recommendations

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:06.520
that went unimplemented. Trust officials and regulators stress that changes already introduced

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:12.340
address many identified problems, both sides accept that multiple prior investigations found

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.060
serious shortcomings, which previous inquiries into the same trust reach similar conclusions.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.400
Meanwhile, energy costs show movement in the United States. Diesel costs in the United States fell

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.400
under $5 a gallon for the first time since mid-March. The decline affects trucking, agriculture,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.500
