00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:08.260
Now to really understand the Senate resolution on Iran, the constitutional mechanics deserve a

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:14.080
closer look because most coverage treats the vote as either a major rebuke or an empty gesture.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:21.020
Article 1 gives Congress the power to declare war and fund military actions while Article 2

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:26.600
designates the president as commander in chief. Resolutions without the force of law sit in the

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:31.960
middle of those authorities. When a non-binding measure passes with bipartisan support,

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.880
it signals to the executive branch that future funding requests or operational expansions may face

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:42.560
legislative resistance, even if the immediate vote changes nothing on the ground.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.680
Knowing this, when you hear claims that the resolution stops military action,

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:52.780
you can evaluate whether the speaker is describing legal effect or political pressure.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.520
Next time you see a headline about congressional pushback on foreign policy,

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:03.700
ask whether the measure a men's statute or simply expresses sentiment and which committees control

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:09.800
the relevant appropriations. Before we go, watch for further updates on nuclear inspection

